The hosted MCP server's image is Inka's, built by every consumer: `packages/inka-mcp/Dockerfile` takes `BUNDLE` (where the deployment's bundled entry is), `PLAYWRIGHT` and `SENTRY`, and ships a `.dockerignore` allow-list beside it, so a consumer deletes its own copy instead of keeping one that drifts. Two consumers held byte-identical copies and had already begun to diverge: one installed the Sentry SDK the bundle leaves external and the other did not. @djay
